# Tomb Dust backlog gate

**Full index:** [`tmp/backlog/README.md`](../../tmp/backlog/README.md) (active) · [`tmp/backlog/closed/`](../../tmp/backlog/closed/README.md) (done/cancelled) · **Template:** [`tmp/backlog/TEMPLATE.md`](../../tmp/backlog/TEMPLATE.md)

## Layout

| Location | Holds |
|----------|--------|
| `tmp/backlog/*.md` | **Active** tickets — `open`, `in_progress` only (plus `TEMPLATE.md`, example ticket) |
| `tmp/backlog/closed/*.md` | **Archived** tickets — `done`, `cancelled` |

## No ticket, no change

Do **not** edit code or canon content unless an **open or in_progress** ticket in `tmp/backlog/` authorizes the work.

| Scope | Rule |
|-------|------|
| **`app/**`** | Must claim ticket first; see **Active session** below |
| **Paths in a ticket's Expected files** | May edit while ticket is active (`open`/`in_progress`) |
| **New behavior** | Create a ticket from [`TEMPLATE.md`](../../tmp/backlog/TEMPLATE.md) first; link a domain spec under `tmp/app-*-spec.md` |
| **Specs only** | Updating `tmp/app-*-spec.md` without code is allowed when syncing after a closed ticket or drafting a new ticket |
| **Dev-team runs** | Artifacts only under `tmp/backlog/runs/APP-XXX-<task>/` per [dev-team SKILL](../../.cursor/skills/dev-team/SKILL.md) |

## Active session (required for `app/` edits)

```bash
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py search --open-only   # new work: open only, not in_progress/done
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py schedule APP-XXX APP-YYY APP-ZZZ   # ≤3, deps
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py claim-batch APP-XXX APP-YYY APP-ZZZ
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py focus APP-XXX
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py impl-check APP-XXX                 # before impl
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py batch-status
python tmp/backlog/claim_ticket.py release APP-XXX --done
```

Writes **`tmp/.active-batch.json`** (≤3 tickets) and **`tmp/.active-ticket.json`** (focus). Session-local, gitignored. Hooks allow `app/` edits when any batch ticket is active.

## Before implementing

1. Run **claim** (sets ticket `in_progress` + optional run folder).
2. Read the ticket's **Domain spec** (`tmp/app-*-spec.md`) — specs remain source of truth for behavior.
3. Stay within **Expected files**; add paths to the ticket before touching others.

## After implementing

1. Check ticket acceptance criteria; mark **Status** → `done` + **Closed** date (or use `release --done` / `release --cancelled` — archives to `tmp/backlog/closed/`).
2. Update domain spec changelog.
3. Run **`release --done`** to clear `tmp/.active-ticket.json`.

## Automated enforcement (Cursor hooks)

See [`.cursor/hooks.json`](../../.cursor/hooks.json):

| Hook | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| `sessionStart` | Injects active ticket + in-progress list |
| `preToolUse` | Denies `Write`/`StrReplace`/… to gated paths without valid claim |
| `subagentStart` | Denies Task subagents unless prompt includes `APP-XXX` or session is claimed |
| `stop` | Warns if `app/` changed in git diff without active ticket |

## Exceptions (no ticket required)

- Edits under `tmp/backlog/`, `tmp/app-*-spec.md`, `.cursor/` (tickets, specs, hooks)
- Typo/format fixes with **zero** behavior change outside `app/` (note in commit message)
- Emergency revert of a broken commit (follow with a ticket for the real fix)
- Reading/exploring code, running tests, or answering questions without edits

## Drift policy (unchanged)

Spec ↔ code drift is never allowed. Tickets track **work**; domain specs track **behavior**. Both update when work lands. See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [`tmp/app-master-spec.md`](../../tmp/app-master-spec.md).
